  "step_3": "The decision reason requires comparing all pairwise outcome differences between the two lotteries and summing them, independent of probabilities. The individual, however, focuses solely on the probability of not losing money (i.e., getting 0 Euros), which is higher in B (55%) than in A (10%). They do not reference the size of the losses in a comparative way that involves calculating differences between outcomes. Instead, they acknowledge the larger loss in B but prioritize the higher chance of avoiding loss. There is no indication that the individual computed or considered all pairwise outcome differences or aggregated them. The justification is probability-based (focusing on likelihood of zero outcome), while the reason is structure-based (focusing on outcome value differences). The information considered by the individual (probabilities of zero) does not match the information required by the reason (outcome values for pairwise comparison). Therefore, there is no evidence the reason was used.",
